  "comment": "Modern Israeli Hebrew, the way it is written on news sites, forums and shops. A word is found behind the prefixes the language glues on (ו, ה, ב, ל, מ, ש, כ) and with or without vowel points, so each form is listed once. Short words that are also ordinary words are left out on purpose: זין is the letter, כוס is a cup, תחת is 'under', שיט is sailing, מין is a kind, מזוין is armed, פטיש is a hammer, שקוף is transparent; and because a prefix letter is allowed in front of every word, זונות is left out (מזונות is the bracha) and so is זיון (בזיון is contempt). Replacements are the formal or milder word, so a news report still reads.",
